module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.SectionsPullbackComparison.GeneratingFamily
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DivisorFlatPullback.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Properties.ExtendFiniteType.QuasiCompactOpenIdeal

/-!
# The inverse image of the image ideal sheaf of a morphism to the structure sheaf

Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a morphism of schemes, let `A` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module and let
`φ : A ⟶ 𝒪_X`. The image of `φ` is the quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals
`AlgebraicGeometry.idealSheafDataOfHom A φ`, whose ideal on an affine open `U` is the range of
`φ` there. This file computes its scheme-theoretic inverse image `(idealSheafDataOfHom A φ)·𝒪_Y`.

On a compatible pair of affine opens — `U ⊆ X` and `V ⊆ Y` with `V ⊆ f⁻¹U` — the answer is the
ideal of `Γ(Y, V)` generated by the pullbacks of the values of `φ` on `Γ(A, U)`. Globally the
answer is again an image ideal sheaf: it is the image of the canonical `f^*A ⟶ 𝒪_Y` obtained
from `φ`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.structureUnitToPushforward`: the comparison `𝒪_X ⟶ f_*𝒪_Y`, as a morphism
  of `𝒪_X`-modules.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackStructureHom`: the pullback `f^*A ⟶ 𝒪_Y` of `φ`, as its adjoint
  transpose along that comparison.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ideal_comap_idealSheafDataOfHom`: **the inverse image on a pair of affine
  charts.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.comap_idealSheafDataOfHom`: the inverse image of an image ideal sheaf is
  the image of any morphism `f^*A ⟶ 𝒪_Y` pulling `φ` back.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.structureAppₗ_pullbackStructureHom`: `pullbackStructureHom` does pull `φ`
  back, in that sense.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.comap_idealSheafDataOfHom_eq_idealSheafDataOfHom_pullback`: **the inverse
  image of an image ideal sheaf is an image ideal sheaf**, with no hypothesis.

## Implementation notes

The chart statement is `Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE` — the ideal of `I·𝒪_Y` on `V` is
the image of the ideal of `I` on `U` under `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.appLE` — applied to an
ideal which is a range, together with `Ideal.map` of a range being the span of the composite
range. No quasi-coherence beyond what `idealSheafDataOfHom` already requires is used.

The global statement is proved first from the pullback `ψ : f^*A ⟶ 𝒪_Y` as data, through the
only property of it the proof uses: that it carries the pullback of a section `x` of `A` over
`U` to the pullback of `φ(x)` along `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.appLE`. The inclusion `⊇` is
where quasi-coherence of `A` is used: the sections of `f^*A` over `V` are spanned over
`Γ(Y, V)` by the pullbacks of the sections of `A` over `U`, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.span_pullbackSection_eq_top`.

`pullbackStructureHom` then supplies that datum, and its defining property is read off the unit
of `f^* ⊣ f_*`: `CategoryTheory.Adjunction.homEquiv_unit` says that the transpose composed with
the unit is what it was transposed from, and `AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackSectionHom` *is* the
unit followed by a restriction, so the two statements differ only by that restriction, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.map_structureAppₗ`. Mathlib's own comparison
`SheafOfModules.pullbackObjUnitToUnit` is not used: its instance arguments are not found at the
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` spelling (the measurement is recorded in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/AffineClosedUnion/TwistedUnit.lean`), whereas
`SheafOfModules.unitToPushforwardObjUnit`, the morphism it is the transpose of, needs none and
is what `structureUnitToPushforward` ascribes at this spelling.

Several steps are `rfl`-ascriptions rather than rewrites, for the reason recorded in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Descent/SectionsPullbackComparison/PullbackSection.lean`: the
sections of `(f^* ⋙ f_*)A` over `U` and of `f^*A` over `f⁻¹U` are definitionally but not
syntactically equal, and a rewrite whose motive mentions both is rejected at `implicit`
transparency.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01BG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01BG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 080B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080B)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerColimit

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The inverse image of a quasi-coherent module is quasi-coherent, at the
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` spelling, so that `AlgebraicGeometry.idealSheafDataOfHom`
applies to it. -/
instance isQuasicoherent_modulesPullbackObj (f : Y ⟶ X) (A : X.Modules) [A.IsQuasicoherent] :
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj A).IsQuasicoherent :=
  @SheafOfModules.modulePullback_isQuasicoherent Y.toRingedSpace X.toRingedSpace
    f.toLRSHom.toShHom A ‹_›

/-- **The inverse image of an image ideal sheaf on a pair of affine charts.** If the affine open
`V` of `Y` lies in the preimage of the affine open `U` of `X`, then the ideal of
`(idealSheafDataOfHom A φ)·𝒪_Y` on `V` is generated by the pullbacks of the values of `φ` on
the sections of `A` over `U`. -/
theorem ideal_comap_idealSheafDataOfHom (A : X.Modules) [A.IsQuasicoherent]
    (φ : A ⟶ structureModule X) (f : Y ⟶ X) (U : X.affineOpens) (V : Y.affineOpens)
    (hVU : (V : Y.Opens) ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ (U : X.Opens)) :
    ((idealSheafDataOfHom A φ).comap f).ideal V =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun x : Γ(A, U.1) ↦
        (f.appLE U.1 V.1 hVU).hom (structureAppₗ φ U.1 x)) := by
  have hmap : ∀ (g : Γ(X, U.1) →+* Γ(Y, V.1)) (K : Ideal Γ(X, U.1)),
      Ideal.map g K = Ideal.span (g '' (K : Set Γ(X, U.1))) := fun _ _ ↦ rfl
  rw [Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE (idealSheafDataOfHom A φ) f U V hVU,
    idealSheafDataOfHom_ideal, hmap, idealOfHom, LinearMap.coe_range, ← Set.range_comp]
  rfl

/-- **The inverse image of an image ideal sheaf is an image ideal sheaf.** For a morphism
`ψ : f^*A ⟶ 𝒪_Y` pulling `φ` back — that is, carrying the pullback of a section `x` of `A` to
the pullback of `φ(x)` — the image of `ψ` is the inverse image of the image of `φ`. -/
theorem comap_idealSheafDataOfHom (f : Y ⟶ X) (A : X.Modules) [A.IsQuasicoherent]
    (φ : A ⟶ structureModule X)
    (ψ : (Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj A ⟶ structureModule Y)
    (hψ : ∀ (U : X.Opens) (V : Y.Opens) (hVU : V ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ U) (x : Γ(A, U)),
      structureAppₗ ψ V (pullbackSectionHom f A U V hVU x) =
        (f.appLE U V hVU).hom (structureAppₗ φ U x)) :
    (idealSheafDataOfHom A φ).comap f =
      idealSheafDataOfHom ((Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj A) ψ := by
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext_of_iSup_eq_top
    (ι := Σ U : X.affineOpens, {V : Y.affineOpens // (V : Y.Opens) ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ (U : X.Opens)})
    (fun i ↦ i.2.1) (top_le_iff.mp fun y _ ↦ ?_) ?_
  · obtain ⟨-, ⟨U, hU, rfl⟩, hyU, -⟩ :=
      X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ (f.base y)) isOpen_univ
    obtain ⟨-, ⟨V, hV, rfl⟩, hyV, hVU⟩ :=
      Y.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (show y ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ U from hyU)
        (f ⁻¹ᵁ U).isOpen
    exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨⟨U, hU⟩, ⟨V, hV⟩, hVU⟩, hyV⟩
  · rintro ⟨U, V, hVU⟩
    rw [ideal_comap_idealSheafDataOfHom A φ f U V hVU, idealSheafDataOfHom_ideal, idealOfHom]
    refine le_antisymm (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_) ?_
    · rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨pullbackSectionHom f A U.1 V.1 hVU x, hψ U.1 V.1 hVU x⟩
    · rintro _ ⟨t, rfl⟩
      have hle : Submodule.span Γ(Y, V.1)
            (Set.range fun x : Γ(A, U.1) ↦ pullbackSectionHom f A U.1 V.1 hVU x) ≤
          Submodule.comap (structureAppₗ ψ V.1)
            (Ideal.span (Set.range fun x : Γ(A, U.1) ↦
              (f.appLE U.1 V.1 hVU).hom (structureAppₗ φ U.1 x))) := by
        rw [Submodule.span_le]
        rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
        refine Submodule.mem_comap.mpr ?_
        rw [hψ U.1 V.1 hVU x]
        exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨x, rfl⟩
      exact hle (by rw [span_pullbackSection_eq_top f A U.2 V.2 hVU]; trivial)

/-! ### The canonical pullback of a morphism to the structure sheaf -/

/-- The canonical comparison `𝒪_X ⟶ f_*𝒪_Y` of a morphism of schemes, read as a morphism of
`𝒪_X`-modules: Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.unitToPushforwardObjUnit`, with its codomain declared
at the `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` spelling. -/
noncomputable def structureUnitToPushforward (f : Y ⟶ X) :
    structureModule X ⟶ (Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj (structureModule Y) :=
  SheafOfModules.unitToPushforwardObjUnit f.toRingCatSheafHom

/-- On sections over `U`, the comparison `𝒪_X ⟶ f_*𝒪_Y` is the ring map `f.app U`. -/
@[simp]
theorem structureUnitToPushforward_app (f : Y ⟶ X) (U : X.Opens) (r : Γ(X, U)) :
    (structureUnitToPushforward f).app U r = f.app U r := rfl

/-- **The pullback of a morphism to the structure sheaf**: the adjoint transpose, under
`f^* ⊣ f_*`, of `φ` followed by the comparison `𝒪_X ⟶ f_*𝒪_Y`. -/
noncomputable def pullbackStructureHom (f : Y ⟶ X) {A : X.Modules}
    (φ : A ⟶ structureModule X) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj A ⟶ structureModule Y :=
  ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).homEquiv A (structureModule Y)).symm
    (φ ≫ structureUnitToPushforward f)

/-- **The pullback of `φ` pulls `φ` back.** On a section of `A` over `U`, the canonical
`f^*A ⟶ 𝒪_Y` takes the pullback of the section to the pullback of its value under `φ`. -/
theorem structureAppₗ_pullbackStructureHom (f : Y ⟶ X) {A : X.Modules}
    (φ : A ⟶ structureModule X) (U : X.Opens) (V : Y.Opens) (hVU : V ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ U) (x : Γ(A, U)) :
    structureAppₗ (pullbackStructureHom f φ) V (pullbackSectionHom f A U V hVU x) =
      (f.appLE U V hVU).hom (structureAppₗ φ U x) := by
  set N := (Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj A with hN
  set ψ := pullbackStructureHom f φ with hψ
  set y : Γ(N, f ⁻¹ᵁ U) :=
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app A).app U x with hy
  have hadj : (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app A ≫
      (Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).map ψ = φ ≫ structureUnitToPushforward f := by
    have h1 : (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).homEquiv A
        (structureModule Y) ψ =
        (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app A ≫
          (Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).map ψ := Adjunction.homEquiv_unit _ _ _ _
    have h2 : (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).homEquiv A
        (structureModule Y) ψ = φ ≫ structureUnitToPushforward f := by
      rw [hψ, pullbackStructureHom]
      exact Equiv.apply_symm_apply _ _
    exact h1.symm.trans h2
  have hL : (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app A ≫
        (Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).map ψ).app U x : Γ(Y, f ⁻¹ᵁ U)) =
      structureAppₗ ψ (f ⁻¹ᵁ U) y := rfl
  have hR : (((φ ≫ structureUnitToPushforward f).app U x : Γ(Y, f ⁻¹ᵁ U))) =
      f.app U (structureAppₗ φ U x) := rfl
  have hU : structureAppₗ ψ (f ⁻¹ᵁ U) y = f.app U (structureAppₗ φ U x) :=
    hL.symm.trans ((congrArg (fun q : A ⟶ (Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj
      (structureModule Y) ↦ (q.app U x : Γ(Y, f ⁻¹ᵁ U))) hadj).trans hR)
  have hres : pullbackSectionHom f A U V hVU x = N.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op y := rfl
  rw [hres, ← map_structureAppₗ ψ hVU, hU, Scheme.Hom.appLE]
  rfl

/-- **The inverse image of an image ideal sheaf, unconditionally.** The inverse image of the
image of `φ : A ⟶ 𝒪_X` is the image of the canonical `f^*A ⟶ 𝒪_Y`. -/
theorem comap_idealSheafDataOfHom_eq_idealSheafDataOfHom_pullback (f : Y ⟶ X) (A : X.Modules)
    [A.IsQuasicoherent] (φ : A ⟶ structureModule X) :
    (idealSheafDataOfHom A φ).comap f =
      idealSheafDataOfHom ((Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj A) (pullbackStructureHom f φ) :=
  comap_idealSheafDataOfHom f A φ _ fun U V hVU x ↦
    structureAppₗ_pullbackStructureHom f φ U V hVU x

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
